How's this for an item: a compass.  If it is a normal compass, it will 
indicate the direction that a down staircase lies (direction to closest
if more than two).  A cursed compass will point you to the up staircase,
or randomly.  A magic compass will act like a crysle ball, but will only
give the direction, not location.

Why have a compass....?  Well, for the following quest.... :)

Imagine 3 levels, each which contain 9 identical rooms (5x5), each which 
contain 'magic portals' that lead to other magic portals in other
rooms.  Portals are two-way.  Enterance is gained to the levels by a magic
portal from the main dungeon tree.  An exit portal is also located somewhere.

Place a minotaur in the maze somewhere, and get a good bunch of wandering
monsters.  The character has to kill the minotaur, take his hide (or some
object), make it to the exit portal, which will only allow one with the 
hide to pass through.  The characer is rewarded with a large room of gold/
treasures/etc :).

If one own a normal compass upon entering the maze, it will tell him where
the room containing the exit is located relative to the current room.  A
magic compass will tell the user which portal to take (ie shortest route)
to get to the exit from the current room.

This would seem like a good quest for levels 7-12  (helping with the 
experience to be able to do the class quest).

